                <pb facs="0626" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg538"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 W 451/161: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-12-09T15:00:00-05:00">December 9, 1933—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>140. Your 501, December 8, 11 a.m. The President asked me to say that he believes
                    it would be well for you to make your plans to leave on the evening of the 12th
                    or the 13th. Caffery is now at his home in Louisiana and will presumably reach
                    Habana a few days after your departure. We all feel that it would be best for
                    him not to give the appearance of hastening to Habana immediately after you have
                    left.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
